WinEDR - Window Electrophysiology Disk Recorder

The files contained in this archive can be buit using Embarcadero Delphi software development environment.
https://www.embarcadero.com/products/delphi/starter

To build and run the application:

1) Clone this repository to a folder in the Delphi XE Projects folder e.g. ..\My Documents\Embarcadero\Studio\Projects\WinEDR<br>
2) Select File > Open Project and open .. \My Documents\Embarcadero\Studio\Projects\WinEDR\WinEDR

Note. The SESComponents package of common Delphi components used in Strathclyde Electrophysiology Software applications must be downloaded from 
https://github.com/johndempster/SESComponentsXE 
and installed on the Delphi toolbar before building this application. See the SESComponentsXE repository  for details.


